id: pm-a7207g
title: "GH-1190: Windows nightly can publish the event index after an unlocked fallback append"
description: "Nightly Validation run 33854480862 on main e486179 failed in Windows Node 24 because the unlocked-fallback append regression resolved instead of rejecting: runtime/history-event-index.json remained physically visible. The prior pm-fqlocp fix made invalidation the portable query invariant but retained a physical-unlink assertion that is nondeterministic under full-suite Windows scheduling. Make the test deterministic without weakening the committed invalidation or incomplete-index refusal contracts, and add it to the required Windows regression gate."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: "area:history","area:tests",ci,windows
created_at: "2026-09-04T13:19:39.118Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-04T13:40:11.393Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-04T13:40:10.772Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-04T13:40:10.772Z"
author: "harness:codex"
parent: pm-o2kc
severity: high
environment: GitHub Actions Nightly Validation windows-latest Node 24 run 33854480862 at e486179
repro_steps: "Run the full nightly suite on Windows Node 24 at e486179; tests/unit/core/history/event-index.spec.ts expects fs.access(runtime/history-event-index.json) to reject after an unlocked fallback append, but Windows can retain the file while committed invalidation correctly prevents queries."
resolution: Replaced nondeterministic physical file-absence verification with the public invalidation/query-refusal invariant and ratcheted the full event-index regression into the required Windows workflow plus workflow contract.
expected_result: "Unlocked fallback appends never expose stale derived-index queries, and every PR proves the behavior on Windows without depending on filesystem delete timing."
actual_result: "The focused event-index and workflow contracts pass, the full 32-test event-index suite passed ten consecutive repetitions, and exact full coverage plus repository static gates pass."
affected_version: 2026.9.4
component: history event index tests and Windows CI
regression: true
customer_impact: A nondeterministic required nightly blocks release confidence and leaves GitHub issue #1190 open even when the derived-index runtime contract is intact.
