comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-04T13:19:39.118Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: all-status search found closed pm-fqlocp as the exact prior defect, open pm-7c27ep as recurrence-policy governance, and open pm-801d as the derived-index feature. This is a verified post-fix recurrence from GitHub issue #1190 and run 33854480862, so it is tracked separately with recurs_from lineage rather than reopening or duplicating the completed fix."
  "2026-09-04T13:21:26.408Z","harness:codex","TDD red evidence: the CI workflow contract now requires tests/unit/core/history/event-index.spec.ts in the required Windows regression job and fails because the current job omits it. Production red evidence remains Nightly run 33854480862: the physical SQLite absence assertion resolved on Windows even though committed invalidation is the portable safety invariant."
  "2026-09-04T13:39:58.924Z","harness:codex","Implementation and verification evidence: the unlocked-fallback regression now asserts queryHistoryEventIndex returns null, the portable public invalidation contract, instead of nondeterministic physical SQLite disappearance. The complete event-index suite passed 10 consecutive 32-test repetitions. The required Windows PR job now runs the full event-index spec and a workflow contract prevents removal. Full coverage passes 603 files and 8,356 tests at exact 100/100/100/100; quality:static, typecheck, docs links, and security scan pass."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-04T13:39:59.476Z","harness:codex","Derived-index safety is defined by refusing stale queries after invalidation, not by immediate physical deletion on every filesystem. Windows delete-pending timing can retain the file transiently, so required Windows CI must exercise the public refusal invariant directly."
